+operations (`get`, orchestration summary, comment list/create, and status update) only
+inside a host-dispatched tool run. The host revalidates the persisted running issue run,
+snapshot, execution binding and assignee on each call; limits targets to the same project
+and the current issue or a direct parent/child; and applies canonical issue privacy and
+read/comment/mutate decisions using the host-derived agent/run. Its orchestration result
+contains only that issue's run and blocker IDs, and the candidate bridge requires the
+reviewer child to depend exactly on its producer before submission. Ordinary SDK calls
+and plugin jobs retain their existing authority. Focused SDK, server and bridge tests pass;
+this remains source-only and does not claim deployed acceptance.
+
 Evidence: `source-only` — [implementation](../../server/src/routes/plugins.ts#L965) at
 the reviewed commit above.
 
